Z||000000||PatrickB||01-19-2001||02:57 AM||||Can anyone tell me the easiest way to disable the cold start valve.  I want to see if that is what is giving me starting problems but I dont want to remove the plenum if I dont have to.<P>Is it plugged into a harness somewhere that I can unplug temporarily?<P>Thanks <P>Pat||||reg||5
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||01-19-2001||06:51 AM||||There is a plug on the valve itself, just like all other injectors. Might be a bit rough getting at, just be careful and don't loose the clip!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tom Philips||01-19-2001||08:45 AM||||There is temperature sensor on the front of the engine that you can unhook wire from it to disable or the 12 volt feed to the injector is on the starter solenoid (fusible link)||||reg||1
Z||000003||ka4nkf||01-19-2001||10:46 PM||||Just a reminder. the cold start valve only works while the starter is engaged.||||reg||1
